{"parentUuid":"25f11420-f836-4cd0-bd50-b28fb3ee7e0d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011W4WcPtwBHPLVd4NchUXhu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A2gPdB9ZcKaEq6NYQwQiGA","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT UNSAT proof restart strategy clause cleanup LBD glucose tuning"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8505,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8505,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqiwWMf2HSBYBWRXwyw","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"98f7c173-357f-468b-b7b7-59c979b6f7ce","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:34.655Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"25f11420-f836-4cd0-bd50-b28fb3ee7e0d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FQwaegV9ieFaDNQqo63zD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT \"search_branching\" PORTFOLIO_SEARCH HINT_SEARCH packing placement performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Value strategy heuristic\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/ba6Gds_qSQY\"},{\"title\":\"How to improve CP-SAT performance for large bin-packing problems? · Issue #1799 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py\"},{\"title\":\"[CP-SAT] Search strategy to find all solutions, but fixing only some variables · Issue #1174 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1174\"},{\"title\":\"How to speed up sat cp using strategies (counting elements in list and adding counts) · Issue #830 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/830\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information about CP-SAT's search branching strategies and their application to packing and placement problems:\n\n## Search Branching Strategies in CP-SAT\n\nCP-SAT provides several search branching options including AUTOMATIC_SEARCH, FIXED_SEARCH, PORTFOLIO_SEARCH, LP_SEARCH, PSEUDO_COST_SEARCH, HINT_SEARCH, and other variants.\n\n### Portfolio-Based Approach\n\nCP-SAT uses a portfolio of different subsolvers, each configured with varying settings (e.g., different levels of linearization) to solve the model. As a portfolio solver, CP-SAT concurrently executes a multitude of diverse algorithms and strategies, with these elements operating largely independently but engaging in information exchange, sharing progress when better solutions emerge or tighter bounds become available.\n\n### Application to Packing Problems\n\nIn packing problems, certain expensive propagation techniques can significantly speed up the search but can also drastically slow it down if misused. This indicates that the choice of search strategy and branching parameters can have significant performance implications for packing and placement problems.\n\n### Search Strategy Options\n\nSearch strategies are mostly linear based including LP_BRANCHING and PSEUDO_COST_BRANCHING, which are among the options available for controlling how the solver branches during its search process.\n\nThe search results show that PORTFOLIO_SEARCH and HINT_SEARCH are specific configuration options for CP-SAT's search_branching parameter, used to guide the solver's decision-making during the search process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"48b46502-c826-4d1a-b59b-f695b1784dc7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:41.362Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"25f11420-f836-4cd0-bd50-b28fb3ee7e0d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"30339149-a05e-40fe-87d2-e1706ec2195f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RdRi42rjvihKynwHBKTZZM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT parameter tuning guide 2025 linearization_level cuts presolve\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-autotune: WIP: Tune the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver for specific models · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.cc at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.cc\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Presolve time limit · google/or-tools · Discussion #4280\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4280\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.h\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about OR-Tools CP-SAT parameter tuning for `linearization_level`, `cuts`, and `presolve`:\n\n## Presolve Parameter Tuning\n\nThe CP-SAT solver includes a presolve step that simplifies the model before solving it. This step can significantly reduce the search space and enhance performance. However, presolve can be time-consuming, particularly for large models.\n\nIf your model is relatively simple and you notice that presolve is taking a long time while the search itself is fast, you might consider reducing the presolve effort. You can limit specific presolve techniques. For instance, you can constrain the time or intensity of probing, which is a technique that tries to fix variables and observe the outcome.\n\nKey presolve-related parameters include:\n- max_presolve_iterations (default: 3), cp_model_probing_level (default: 2), presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit (default: 30.0)\n\n## Linearization and Cuts\n\nCP-SAT uses a portfolio of different subsolvers, each configured with varying settings (e.g., different levels of linearization) to solve the model. \n\nThe cut_level parameter sets the level of effort the solver will invest in generating cutting planes, which are linear constraints added to remove fractional solutions. At root level, even cutting planes such as Gomory-Cuts are applied to improve the linear relaxation.\n\n## Important Warning About Parameter Modification\n\nIt is important not to modify the parameters at the top level, as this would affect all subsolvers, including the LNS-workers. Doing so could disrupt the balance of the portfolio, potentially activating costly techniques for the LNS-workers, which could slow them down.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"20b38cc3-c750-4beb-b0e4-dd3e588d8e86","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:41.904Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30339149-a05e-40fe-87d2-e1706ec2195f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98f7c173-357f-468b-b7b7-59c979b6f7ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A2gPdB9ZcKaEq6NYQwQiGA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT UNSAT proof restart strategy clause cleanup LBD glucose tuning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"On the Glucose SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://univ-artois.hal.science/hal-03299473v1/document\"},{\"title\":\"On the Glucose SAT Solver Gilles Audemard\",\"url\":\"https://univ-artois.hal.science/hal-03299473/document\"},{\"title\":\"Refining Restarts Strategies for SAT and UNSAT | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-33558-7_11\"},{\"title\":\"Reﬁning restarts strategies for SAT and UNSAT\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/articles/xxmain.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Glucose for Incremental SAT Solving with Assumptions: Application to MUS Extraction | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-39071-5_23\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning-Based Restart Policy for CDCL SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-94144-8_6\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - audemard/glucose: The glucose SAT solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/audemard/glucose\"},{\"title\":\"Tuning Parallel SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://easychair.org/publications/download/NkG7\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Glucose for Incremental SAT Solving with ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/articles/xmain.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the topics covered in your query:\n\n## Glucose SAT Solver Techniques\n\n**LBD (Literal Block Distance):**\nLBD is a quality measure that has been proven to be very informative in practice to predict clauses usefulness. Given a conflict graph, any First UIP asserting clause has the smallest LBD value over all other UIPs.\n\n**Clause Cleanup and Aggressive Deletion:**\nIn most cases for \"Industrial\" problems it seems crucial to aggressively remove many learnt clauses, even during the first conflicts (up to 95% of them). Two factors seem to play a crucial role in managing the learnt clause database: keeping as few clauses as possible ensures a very fast BCP, and removing bad clauses allows to guide the solver search around a shorter UNSAT proof.\n\n**Restart Strategy:**\nThe restart policy introduced in glucose, and based on the quality of recently learnt clauses, has been proven to be very efficient in practice. This restart scheme is particularly efficient on unsatisfiable instances.\n\n**Tuning Parameters:**\nIn the first version of glucose (2009), X = 100 and K = 0.7 were experimentally fixed to give good results on both SAT and UNSAT problems. These values were changed (X = 50 and K = 0.8) since the version 2.1 of glucose (2012).\n\nThe search results provide detailed information about Glucose's techniques but contain limited specific information about CP-SAT's particular implementations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"52217258-114e-4bf6-abaa-884ea8674e18","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:42.893Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98f7c173-357f-468b-b7b7-59c979b6f7ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a87ba485-c61a-4a5a-8737-db64e19ac898","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LwxaA8AX4ATQwBsHL5a19f","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Key Parameters Summary\n\n## Restart Strategy\n\n**restart_algorithms** (repeated RestartAlgorithm)\n- Default: \"LUBY_RESTART,LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART,DL_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART\"\n- Switches strategies as counter increments; NO_RESTART prevents further changes\n\n**restart_period** (int32)\n- Default: 50\n- Multiplier for LUBY_RESTART; trigger period for FIXED_RESTART\n\n**restart_dl_average_ratio** (double)\n- Default: 1.0\n- For DL moving average: restart when window average × ratio exceeds global average\n\n**restart_lbd_average_ratio** (double)\n- Default: 1.0\n- For LBD moving average: restart when window average × ratio exceeds global average\n\n## Clause Learning & Cleanup\n\n**clause_cleanup_period** (int32)\n- Default: 10000\n- Triggers cleanup after this many deletable clauses learned\n\n**clause_cleanup_target** (int32)\n- Default: 0\n- Clauses to keep during cleanup; if 0, uses clause_cleanup_ratio instead\n\n**clause_cleanup_ordering** (ClauseOrdering enum)\n- Default: CLAUSE_ACTIVITY\n- Options: CLAUSE_ACTIVITY (by decreasing activity then LBD) or CLAUSE_LBD (by increasing LBD)\n\n**clause_cleanup_lbd_bound** (int32)\n- Default: 5\n- Clauses with LBD ≤ this are always protected during cleanup\n\n**glucose_max_decay** (double)\n- Default: 0.95\n- Variable activity decay increases from 0.8 to this value over 5000 conflicts\n\n## Presolve\n\n**presolve_substitution_level** (int32)\n- Default: 1\n- Controls free variable aggregation; 0 disables, positive enables\n\n**presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit** (double)\n- Default: 30.0\n- Max deterministic time for probing in SAT presolve\n\n**presolve_blocked_clause** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Uses heuristic to detect basic blocked clause cases\n\n**presolve_use_bva** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Enables Bounded Variable Addition\n\n**presolve_bve_threshold** (int32)\n- Default: 500\n- Max product of positive/negative occurrences for Bounded Variable Elimination\n\n**inprocessing_dtime_ratio** (double)\n- Default: 0.2\n- Proportion of deterministic time for inprocessing at each restart\n\n**max_presolve_iterations** (int32)\n- Default: 3\n- Maximum iterations when large reductions detected\n\n## Cuts\n\n**add_clique_cuts** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Generates cuts from binary implication graph including learned clauses\n\n**add_lin_max_cuts** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Creates cuts for lin_max constraints per Anderson et al. formulations\n\n**add_objective_cut** (bool)\n- Default: false\n- Forces linear objective ≥ fractional LP value rounded up\n\n**add_zero_half_cuts** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Generates Zero-Half cuts at root node\n\n**add_mir_cuts** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Generates Mixed Integer Rounding cuts at root\n\n**add_rlt_cuts** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Generates Reformulation Linearization Technique cuts (experimental)\n\n**cut_active_count_decay** (double)\n- Default: 0.8\n- Decay parameter for cut activity tracking\n\n**cut_level** (int32)\n- Default: 1\n- Controls global cut effort; 0 disables all cuts\n\n## Search Strategy\n\n**search_branching** (SearchBranching enum)\n- Default: AUTOMATIC_SEARCH\n- Options include FIXED_SEARCH, LP_SEARCH, PSEUDO_COST_SEARCH, HINT_SEARCH\n\n**randomize_search** (bool)\n- Default: false\n- Randomizes fixed search heuristics\n\n**linearization_level** (int32)\n- Default: 1\n- 0: no LP; 1: linear + full encoding; 2: adds Boolean constraints\n\n**instantiate_all_variables** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Adds default integer branching to fix remaining variables\n\n**polarity_rephase_increment** (int32)\n- Default: 1000\n- Changes polarity heuristic after this many conflicts (x, 2x, etc.)\n\n**use_phase_saving** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Uses literal phase saving from longest non-conflicting assignments\n\n## LP Relaxation\n\n**mip_max_bound** (double)\n- Default: 1e7\n- Maximum variable magnitude for CP-SAT conversion from MIP\n\n**use_implied_bounds** (bool)\n- Default: true\n- Stores and exploits relations like literal → (var ≥ bound) for cuts\n\n**root_lp_iterations** (int32)\n- Default: 2000\n- Max LP iterations per chunk at root; continues in tree or next root visit\n\n## Optimization\n\n**binary_minimization_algorithm** (BinaryMinizationAlgorithm enum)\n- Default: BINARY_MINIMIZATION_FROM_UIP_AND_DECISIONS\n- Exploits binary clauses to minimize learned clauses further\n\n**optimize_with_core** (bool)\n- Default: false\n- Uses core-based approach (like max-SAT) instead of linear scan for lower bounds\n\n**optimize_with_max_hs** (bool)\n- Default: false\n- Hybrid MIP/CP core-based algorithm similar to max-HS for max-SAT\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The proto file contains 356 total parameters. Many specialized parameters for scheduling, no-overlap constraints, and routing problems exist but were excluded per focus criteria."}]},"uuid":"e635e338-4450-4881-a8bd-e4aa31ebf3c4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:47.021Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a87ba485-c61a-4a5a-8737-db64e19ac898","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
