{"parentUuid":"541fe581-4d41-4a4d-acb7-f035c093af9d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ExqEK2YUr8rYWBUrC6rgnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BgGj93ZwkVhasTF1kKW9dG","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html","prompt":"Extract all CP-SAT parameter tuning recommendations. Specifically: which parameters are most worth tuning, what are recommended non-default values, and warnings about parameters that interact badly with num_search_workers > 1. Include specific advice on linearization_level, cp_model_probing_level, repair_hint, use_lns_only, max_presolve_iterations, optimize_with_core, search_branching, and any UNSAT-specific advice."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2925,"cache_read_input_tokens":21618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2925,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoqkw1QTo5P9csp5WDMo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c1e59a7-cf10-4038-844a-8d8238a1b98a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:53.513Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2c1e59a7-cf10-4038-844a-8d8238a1b98a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ExqEK2YUr8rYWBUrC6rgnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H4GU393pvzcyrxTKj7nnR4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune","prompt":"Extract: what auto-tuning approach is used, which CP-SAT parameters does it tune by default, what dependencies (SMAC?), how to use it, and example results showing speedups."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2925,"cache_read_input_tokens":21618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2925,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoqkw1QTo5P9csp5WDMo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"090ee106-ca3d-4000-ae87-0d268bfe7f39","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:54.952Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"090ee106-ca3d-4000-ae87-0d268bfe7f39","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ExqEK2YUr8rYWBUrC6rgnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CNBVJVN7vwjuxzfQvB3UYr","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799","prompt":"Extract Laurent Perron's recommendations for CP-SAT parameters on bin-packing problems. What parameter values does he recommend, and what does he say about FIXED_SEARCH vs PORTFOLIO, linearization_level, and other parameters?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2925,"cache_read_input_tokens":21618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2925,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoqkw1QTo5P9csp5WDMo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"116ab1c9-4330-47ec-8e58-93aa73c2ff31","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:56.890Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"116ab1c9-4330-47ec-8e58-93aa73c2ff31","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ExqEK2YUr8rYWBUrC6rgnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nnms4sse8n2STZHe2XnzqT","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT use_lns_only repair_hint stop_after_first_solution parameters 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2925,"cache_read_input_tokens":21618,"output_tokens":701,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2925},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4025,"output_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":21618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2925,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoqkw1QTo5P9csp5WDMo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cee309b9-3d2e-45b6-ae3f-0360d1849ec0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:57.471Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2c1e59a7-cf10-4038-844a-8d8238a1b98a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgGj93ZwkVhasTF1kKW9dG","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Parameter Tuning Recommendations\n\n## Most Worth Tuning\n\n**`max_time_in_seconds`**: The document emphasizes this as \"suitable for beginners\" and recommends starting with 60-300 seconds for model testing.\n\n**`log_search_progress`**: Described as \"crucial at the beginning,\" enabling visibility into solver behavior during development.\n\n**`num_workers`**: Recommended for manual adjustment. The primer notes that \"reducing the number of workers can actually improve runtime for some problems\" by allowing remaining workers higher frequency and more memory bandwidth.\n\n## Recommended Non-Default Values\n\n- **`relative_gap_limit`**: Set to 0.05 (5%) to stop when provably within 5% of optimum\n- **`cp_model_probing_level`**: Reduce to 1 if presolve dominates runtime\n- **`max_presolve_iterations`**: Limit to 3 if presolve is slow relative to search\n- **`log_to_stdout`**: Set False if using custom `log_callback` (especially in Jupyter)\n\n## Critical Warnings About Multi-Worker Interactions\n\n**Do NOT modify top-level parameters with `num_workers > 1`**: The document warns that changing parameters at solver level \"would affect all subsolvers, including the LNS-workers\" and could \"disrupt the balance of the portfolio,\" potentially activating expensive techniques that \"slow them down to the point of being ineffective.\"\n\nInstead: Add custom subsolvers via `subsolver_params` to test configurations safely on single workers.\n\n## Parameters NOT Addressed\n\nThe document does not discuss `linearization_level`, `repair_hint`, `use_lns_only`, `optimize_with_core`, or UNSAT-specific advice. It briefly mentions `use_lns_only = True` requires a time limit (stateless solver), and notes `search_branching = FIXED_SEARCH` can force strategy adherence—but provides no tuning recommendations for these."}]},"uuid":"e050706b-bc02-410b-aeb4-8960b82b9f40","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:01.124Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2c1e59a7-cf10-4038-844a-8d8238a1b98a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"090ee106-ca3d-4000-ae87-0d268bfe7f39","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4GU393pvzcyrxTKj7nnR4","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT AutoTune: Hyperparameter Optimization Approach\n\n## Auto-Tuning Methodology\n\nThe project employs **Optuna** (not SMAC) for hyperparameter optimization. As stated in the documentation: \"leverages the `optuna` optimization library to systematically explore and suggest optimal hyperparameter configurations tailored to your needs.\"\n\nThe system takes multiple samples per trial to address CP-SAT's high variance, then refines results by identifying statistically significant parameter changes from defaults.\n\n## Default Parameters Tuned\n\nThe library focuses on a curated set of parameters known to be impactful, including:\n- `cp_model_probing_level` (presolve probing intensity)\n- `cut_level` (cutting plane generation effort)\n- Parameters for `no_overlap` constraints\n\nVersion 0.6.0 adopted \"parameters suggested in CPMPy as default,\" indicating community-validated selections rather than exhaustive tuning of all available parameters.\n\n## Key Dependencies\n\n- **optuna** (hyperparameter optimization framework)\n- **Google OR-Tools** (CP-SAT solver)\n- Python-based implementation\n\n## Usage Methods\n\nTwo primary tuning approaches are provided:\n\n1. **`tune_time_to_optimal`**: Minimizes time to find proven optimal solutions\n2. **`tune_for_quality_within_timelimit`**: Maximizes solution quality under strict time constraints\n\n## Example Results\n\nFrom the documented output, tuning achieved approximately **70% reduction** in solving time:\n- Default parameters: mean 1.61 seconds\n- Optimized parameters: mean 0.48 seconds\n- Verification: 20 samples each\n\nThe tool emphasizes these are suggestions requiring validation on larger datasets to avoid overfitting risks."}]},"uuid":"d96adb69-71df-49f2-a384-b73bd5fc822b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:02.918Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"090ee106-ca3d-4000-ae87-0d268bfe7f39","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"116ab1c9-4330-47ec-8e58-93aa73c2ff31","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNBVJVN7vwjuxzfQvB3UYr","type":"tool_result","content":"I've reviewed the provided web page content, which is a GitHub issue (#1799) from the OR-Tools repository discussing CP-SAT performance challenges with large bin-packing problems.\n\nHowever, **the page content does not include any responses or recommendations from Laurent Perron** (the assigned maintainer). The issue only contains the original problem description and code example from the user reporting the performance issue.\n\nTo find Laurent Perron's specific recommendations regarding CP-SAT parameters like FIXED_SEARCH vs PORTFOLIO, linearization_level, and other tuning options for bin-packing problems, you would need to:\n\n1. Check the comments/responses section of that GitHub issue (which isn't included in the provided content)\n2. Search OR-Tools documentation directly\n3. Review other related issues or pull requests he may have commented on\n\nThe current excerpt ends with the issue description and doesn't contain any expert guidance on parameter configuration."}]},"uuid":"1b6c2d9b-0daa-4299-8fe7-77dac18e9afa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:03.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"116ab1c9-4330-47ec-8e58-93aa73c2ff31","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cee309b9-3d2e-45b6-ae3f-0360d1849ec0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nnms4sse8n2STZHe2XnzqT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT use_lns_only repair_hint stop_after_first_solution parameters 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"\\\"Infeasible LNS solution\\\" on CP-SAT model · Issue #4099 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4099\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"🎓 How the CP-SAT solver works | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/explaining-cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"Consistently causing solver to terminate with \\\"Infeasible LNS solution\\\". · Issue #3965 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3965\"}]\n\nI found search results related to CP-SAT parameters. Here's what I found:\n\n## use_lns_only\n\nYou can run only the incomplete subsolvers by setting solver.parameters.use_lns_only = True, but this needs to be combined with a time limit, as the incomplete subsolvers do not know when to stop.\n\n## repair_hint\n\nWhile the search results mention hints in the context of solution hints, they reference the `add_hint()` method rather than a specific \"repair_hint\" parameter. If you have a good intuition about how the solution might look—perhaps from solving a similar model or using a good heuristic—you can inform CP-SAT to incorporate this knowledge into its search. Some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve the solver's performance if they are good.\n\n## stop_after_first_solution\n\nThe search results show this parameter being used in solver configurations. In one example, stop_after_first_solution: false is listed among solver parameters.\n\nThe search results do contain references to these CP-SAT parameters, though they don't provide comprehensive 2025-specific documentation. For the most current and complete parameter documentation, you may want to check the official OR-Tools GitHub repository or the official Google OR-Tools documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d2ad0f66-9f10-482e-89fd-754329279d56","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:04.007Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cee309b9-3d2e-45b6-ae3f-0360d1849ec0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
