{"parentUuid":"d4aa03a4-33af-4248-8c3b-9a55a87053b5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RJR88T6EVWrxtjAK1fAFYo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017LS7rjCK4dSK1VE1JxhAhk","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"add_objective_cut\" \"use_objective_lb_search\" CP-SAT lazy bound improvement"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7565,"cache_read_input_tokens":24543,"output_tokens":565,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7565},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":24543,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7565,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqnBtP3Qthff1STWhGk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6238d3c4-bb2b-436f-88e6-5f8cb688f427","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:14.726Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"91a22e7e-ea25-414a-8962-3bc4db667f63","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JyRho7yACW66Pzfic8ix6k","type":"tool_result","content":"# Limitations of the Source Material\n\nI cannot extract the specific technical advice you've requested because **the provided webpage content does not contain detailed information about those parameters**.\n\n## What the content covers:\n\nThe page discusses CP-SAT's high-level architecture as a portfolio solver using Lazy Clause Generation, its preprocessing steps, and general limitations. It mentions that:\n\n- \"Several full subsolvers, each using a unique strategy, are run across different threads\"\n- Linear relaxations and cutting planes are employed, but details are minimal\n- The page references external resources (proto files, source code, talks) where parameter details would be found\n\n## What's missing:\n\nThe document provides no guidance on:\n- `linearization_level`, `cut_level`, `repair_hint`, or other specific parameters you mentioned\n- How individual subsolvers handle UNSAT proofs versus solution-finding\n- Parameter interactions with multi-worker portfolio settings\n- Domain-specific advice for placement, packing, or grid problems\n\n## Recommendation:\n\nFor the technical parameter advice you seek, you would need to consult:\n- The referenced proto-file of parameters\n- The complete source code repository\n- The developer talks linked in the learning path section\n\nThis source material focuses on conceptual understanding rather than parameter tuning."}]},"uuid":"3defd9ce-25b5-4f3f-90e0-d6882d81d2f1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:16.934Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"91a22e7e-ea25-414a-8962-3bc4db667f63","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d4aa03a4-33af-4248-8c3b-9a55a87053b5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MMkXdvu8ueAFukH6tsjbWW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT subsolver_params extra_subsolvers ignore_subsolvers customize portfolio\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Force CP-SAT to use some specific subsolvers.\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/_UOHuLu7Nws\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Infeasibility Subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tz8ovW6cZtY\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.cc at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.cc\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT subsolver parameters:\n\n## Key Parameters for Customizing the Subsolver Portfolio\n\nYou can control the full solvers with parameters including: `subsolvers` (for clean replacement), `extra_subsolvers`, and `ignore_subsolvers` which tweak the list of subsolvers.\n\n## How the Subsolver Portfolio Works\n\nCP-SAT uses a portfolio of different subsolvers, each configured with varying settings (e.g., different levels of linearization) to solve the model. You can also define your own subsolver with a specific configuration.\n\n## Important Considerations\n\nIt is important not to modify the parameters at the top level, as this would affect all subsolvers, including the LNS-workers, potentially disrupting the balance of the portfolio and causing most or all subsolvers to be excluded from the portfolio, resulting in a solver that is either inefficient or nonfunctional.\n\n## Adding Custom Subsolvers\n\nYou can add a single subsolver that applies specific techniques, and if the parameters do not help, only one worker will be slowed down while the rest of the portfolio remains unaffected, but if the parameters are beneficial, that worker can share its solutions and bounds with the rest of the portfolio, boosting overall performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d15088fe-69df-472c-a29c-566675ec8c81","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:20.330Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4aa03a4-33af-4248-8c3b-9a55a87053b5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e66b921c-3068-4758-a421-2502d60d1659","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tj9WPRZZWysmLNDrr4LQQk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"linearization_level\" 2 packing CP-SAT no_overlap placement grid speedup\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to improve CP-SAT performance for large bin-packing problems? · Issue #1799 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter documentation NoOverlap2D, Cumulative · google/or-tools · Discussion #3107\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3107\"},{\"title\":\"Splitting of noOverlap constraint improves performance · Issue #2423 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2423\"},{\"title\":\"The chore of packing just got faster and easier | MIT News | Massachusetts Institute of Technology\",\"url\":\"https://news.mit.edu/2023/chore-packing-just-got-faster-and-easier-0706\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Rectangles packing grid - Classiq\",\"url\":\"https://docs.classiq.io/latest/explore/applications/optimization/rectangles_packing/rectangles_packing_grid/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about your query regarding linearization_level, packing, CP-SAT, no_overlap, placement, grid, and speedup:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Linearization Level Parameter:**\nThe `linearization_level` parameter can be set to disable linearisation (default: 1, can also set to 2). In default parameters for OR-Tools, linearization_level is set to 1.\n\n**Packing with CP-SAT:**\nCP-SAT offers the following three constraints for intervals: add_no_overlap, add_no_overlap_2d, add_cumulative. add_no_overlap is used to prevent overlaps between intervals on a single dimension, e.g., time. add_no_overlap_2d is used to prevent overlaps between intervals on two dimensions.\n\n**Performance and Grid Placement:**\nIn earlier versions of CP-SAT, the performance of no-overlap constraints was greatly influenced by the resolution. This impact has evolved, yet it remains somewhat inconsistent. For version 9.3, there is a noticeable increase in execution time as the resolution grows. Conversely, in version 9.8, execution time actually reduces when the resolution is higher.\n\n**Speedup Techniques:**\nDecomposing scheduling problems with noOverlap constraint to smaller noOverlap constraints is faster.\n\nThe search results suggest that the linearization_level parameter affects how CP-SAT processes constraints, and the performance of no_overlap constraints in packing problems can be influenced by resolution settings and constraint decomposition strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b01d89ba-7496-44ea-a071-ecb367fee25f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:21.073Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e66b921c-3068-4758-a421-2502d60d1659","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6238d3c4-bb2b-436f-88e6-5f8cb688f427","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"aa32783403f3cf351","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LS7rjCK4dSK1VE1JxhAhk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"add_objective_cut\" \"use_objective_lb_search\" CP-SAT lazy bound improvement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"BestObjectiveBound - How to use it\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/V4GUqACoeKY\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"class Model - Python MIP Documentation - Read the Docs\",\"url\":\"https://python-mip.readthedocs.io/en/latest/classes.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-objective optimization with CP-Sat · Issue #1344 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1344\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the Power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221353593_Lazy_Clause_Generation_Combining_the_Power_of_SAT_and_CP_and_MIP_Solving\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about these CP-SAT related terms:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**`objective_lb_search`**: This solver is focused on improving the bound by disproving the feasibility of the current lower bound. It's one of the full problem subsolvers available in CP-SAT that prioritizes improving the proven objective bound rather than finding better solutions.\n\n**Lazy Bound Improvement**: The concept appears to relate to how CP-SAT incrementally improves bounds during the search process. By disproving the feasibility of the cheapest nodes in the search tree, it incrementally improves the bound, but has only little chances to find better solutions.\n\n**Related Concepts**: The search results also mention that in the example provided, 'objective_lb_search' contributed to improving objective bounds during the solving process.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about `add_objective_cut` or detailed technical documentation about how `use_objective_lb_search` relates to lazy bound improvement in the optimization process. These appear to be implementation-level parameters or methods in CP-SAT that would benefit from consulting the official Google OR-Tools documentation or the solver's source code for more detailed technical information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9f59fe18-e792-4f63-88e9-ad71e44a1e4b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:21.288Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6238d3c4-bb2b-436f-88e6-5f8cb688f427","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
